     "question": "A medium was inoculated with 6 x 10^3 bacteria and at the end had 1.2 x 10^7 bacteria. Using k = 0.963 and Nt = N0 e^(kt), calculate the incubation time t.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "About 7.89 hours (t = ln(2000) / 0.963).",
     "steps": [
      "Use the exponential growth equation Nt = N0 x e^(kt) (the standard form for this equation).",
      "Rearrange: t = ln(Nt / N0) / k.",
      "Nt / N0 = 1.2 x 10^7 / 6 x 10^3 = 2000, and ln(2000) = 7.601.",
      "t = 7.601 / 0.963 = 7.89 hours."
     ],
